# AutomaticNightLight

**AutomaticNightLight** is an Arduino project that turns an LED on automatically when the room is dark and adds a smooth “breathing” fade effect. It also supports an optional push button to toggle between AUTO mode and FORCE ON.

## Behavior
- Bright room → LED OFF
- Dark room → LED breathes (smooth fade in/out)
- Optional button → toggles FORCE ON / AUTO

## Parts
- Arduino Uno / Nano (or compatible)
- 1× LED
- 1× 220Ω resistor (LED)
- 1× LDR (photoresistor)
- 1× 10kΩ resistor (LDR voltage divider)
- (Optional) 1× push button + jumper wires

## Wiring

### LED (PWM)
- D9 → 220Ω resistor → LED anode (+)
- LED cathode (-) → GND

### LDR voltage divider to A0
- 5V → LDR → node → 10kΩ → GND
- node → A0

### Optional button (internal pull-up)
- One side of button → D2
- Other side of button → GND

## Run
1. Open `src/auto_night_light.ino` in Arduino IDE.
2. Select board + port.
3. Upload.
4. Cover the LDR to simulate darkness.

## Tuning
- `DARK_THRESHOLD` controls when it turns on.
- `FADE_STEP` and `FADE_DELAY_MS` control breathing speed.
- Use Serial Monitor (9600 baud) to view LDR readings.

